1 NOTE THEOS; KING OF SYRIA 261-246 BC; b. 286-(KILLED BY HIS WIFE) 246 BC AT EPHESUS,
2 CONT SUCCEEDED BY SON SELEUCUS II CALLINICUS
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT http://www.american-pictures.com/genealogy/persons/per00567.htm#0
1 NOTE Antiochus II, called Theos ("the divine") (circa 287-246 bc), king of 
2 CONT Syria (261-246 bc), son and successor of Antiochus I. The citizens of 
2 CONT Miletus, in Asia Minor, called him Theos after he freed them from the 
2 CONT tyrant Timarchus (flourished 3d century bc) in 258 bc. Having fought a 
2 CONT long and costly war (260-255 bc) against Ptolemy II, king of Egypt, 
2 CONT Antiochus won back most of the territories his father had lost, only to be 
2 CONT defeated in 250 bc by his own satrap, or provincial governor, Diodotus I 
2 CONT (reigned about 256-235 bc), who seized the Syrian province of Bactria. 
2 CONT Subsequently, Antiochus also lost the province of Parthia to the Parthian 
2 CONT dynasty of the Arsacids.
1 NOTE Antiochus II Theos (286-246 BC reigned 261 - 246 BC), whose mother wasthe Macedonian princess Stratonice, daughter of Demetrius Poliorcetes,succeeded his father Antiochus I Soter as head of the Seleucid dynasty on261 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited a state of war with Egypt, which went on along the coasts ofAsia Minor (the "Second Syrian War"). Antiochus also made some attempt toget a footing in Thrace. During the war he was given the title "Theos"which means "G
2 CONC od" in Greek.
2 CONT
2 CONT About 250 BC peace was concluded between Antiochus and Ptolemy II,Antiochus repudiating his wife Laodice and marrying Ptolemy's daughterBerenice, but by 246 BC Antiochus had left Berenice and her infant son inAntioch to live again
2 CONC  with Laodice in Asia Minor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Laodice poisoned him and proclaimed her son Seleucus II Callinicus(reigned 246-225 BC) king.
2 CONT
2 CONT This entry is based on one from the 1911 Encyclopedia Britannica.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Antiochus Theos name is also revealing. Antiochus meant "against" or"instead of." Theos is the Greek word for God. So together the name means"instead of" "God" or "Antichrist." Loadice was married to Antichrist.Antiochus assumed t
2 CONC he name "Theos" after stealing some of Ptolemy's"Philadelphus" people. (This is the man called the King of the South inthe Book of Daniel or the King of Egypt). After winning these people from"Philadelphus" he thinks he is God. Th
2 CONC is has its parallel in theLaodicean church. Many of the people who make up its ranks are people andlocal churches stolen from "the Philadelphia Church."
