2 CONT *** [4] Alexander is not named by Polybius as a victim of the purge of 221. Since Ptolemy IV was apparently removing all potential dynastic threats at this time, including his mother and even his uncle Lysimachus, it hardly seems 
2 CONC likely that he would have left Alexander alone if he was still alive. Hence my conclusion that he died at this time or earlier. Ý
