2 CONC inscriptions stating his donations in Athens and Delos and had great veneration in which he kept for the Greek God Apollo. At the Capitoline Museums in Rome, is on a display a bilingual inscription dedication to him. Mithridates V
2 CONC  was buried in the royal tombs of his ancestors at Amasya.
