2 CONT =Seleucus V Philometor=
2 CONT
2 CONT The Seleucid king '''Seleucus V Philometor''' (126 - 125 BC), ruler of the Hellenistic Seleucid kingdom, was the eldest son of '''Demetrius II Nicator''' and '''Cleopatra Thea'''.[1] The epithet Philometor means mother-loving and 
2 CONC in the Hellenistic world usually indicated that the mother acted as co-regent for the prince.
2 CONT In 126 BC '''Demetrios II''' was murdered at the instigation of his wife Cleopatra Thea. Now she herself took power and soon also killed her oldest surviving son '''Seleucus V'''. Two different motives are given as reason for this
2 CONC  deed: According to one version he had attempted to claim the throne without her agreement,[2] according to the other version she was afraid that he might avenge the assassination of his father.[3]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Seleucus V Philometor=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT The Seleucid king Seleucus V Philometor (Greek: Σέλευκος Ε΄ ὁ Φιλομήτωρ; 126-125 BC), ruler of the Hellenistic Seleucid kingdom, was the eldest son of Demetrius II Nicator and Cleopatra Thea. The epithet Philometor means "mother-l
2 CONC oving" and in the Hellenistic world usually indicated that the mother acted as co-regent for the prince.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 126 BC Demetrios II was murdered at the instigation of his wife, Cleopatra Thea. Now she herself took power and soon also killed her oldest surviving son Seleucus V. Two different motives are given as reason for this deed: Acco
2 CONC rding to one version he had attempted to claim the throne without her agreement, according to the other version she was afraid that he might avenge the assassination of his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucus_V_Philometor
