1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In Greek sources,[1] '''Ostanes''' is given as the name of one of the sons of the Achaemenid Persian emperor Darius (II) Nothos, and the grandfather of Darius (III) Codomannos. Aside from the name and relationship 
2 CONC to the rulers, the sources do not have any information about the person.
2 CONT
2 CONT The sources are Diodorus 17.5.5 and Plutarch Artax. 1.1.5. The latter explicitly names Ctesias (the physician of Artaxerxes (II) Mnemon) as his source. Ctesias, however, names Artostes as the son of Darius II, and Ferdinand Justi 
2 CONC suggests that the sources confused Artostes as Ostanes.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostanes_(son_of_Darius_II)
