1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the late 4th century BCE through early 3rd century BCE, Amastris, wife of Dionysius of Heraclea, conquered four settlements and united them into a new city-state named after her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Amastris (Greek: Ἄμαστρις; murdered c. 284 BC), also called Amastrine, was a Persian princess and ruler of the city of Heracleia. As such, she was the first queen to issue coins in her name. He also founded an eponymous city
2 CONC , Amastris, today Amasara, in Paphlagonia, Anatolia.1​  Wikipedia
