1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyrus_the_Great Cyrus the Great, From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT According to [http://www.geni.com/people/Plutarch/6000000011267572005 Plutarch], ( [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plutarch Wikipedia Link] ) , his epitaph said,
2 CONT
2 CONT O man, whoever you are and wherever you come from, for I know you will come, I am Cyrus who won the Persians their empire. Do not therefore begrudge me this bit of earth that covers my bones.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cyrus II, The Great, King of Persia, was born circa 600 BC, Anshan, Persia; died circa December, 530 BC, along the Syr Darya.
2 CONT
