1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mithridates IV Aršakuni was King (or anti-King) between 128 and 147. He was the brother of Osroes I of Parthia (109–129). During the invasion of Mesopotamia by the Roman Emperor Trajan (98–117) in 116 he and his so
2 CONC n Sanatruces II took up the diadem but were defeated. After the death of Osroes I in 129 he assumed the throne and continued the struggle with the rival king Vologases III of Parthia (105–147), our ancestor. Mithridates died in an
2 CONC  attack on Commagene in 140. Mithridates IV had appointed his son Sanatruces successor, but Sanatruces fell in a battle with the Romans. Another son, Vologases IV of Parthia (147–191), took the throne after the death of Vologases 
2 CONC III in 147.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithridates_IV_of_Parthia
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Mithridates IV of Parthia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Mithridates IV of Parthia (flourished 1st century & 2nd century) was a Prince of Iranian and Greek ancestry. He ruled as King of the Parthian Empire from 129 to 140. Mithridates IV was the youngest son born to Vonones II from a Gr
2 CONC eek concubine and was one of the brothers of Osroes I of Parthia (109-129). During the invasion of Mesopotamia by the Roman emperor Trajan (98-117) in 116, he and his son Sanatruces II of Parthia, took up the diadem but were defea
2 CONC ted. After the death of Osroes I in 129 he assumed the throne and continued the struggle with the rival King Vologases III of Parthia (105-147). He died in an attack on Commagene in 140. Mithridates IV had appointed his son Sanatr
2 CONC uces II as his successor, but Sanatruces II fell in a battle with the Romans. Another son, Vologases IV of Parthia (147-191), took the throne after the death of Vologases III in 147.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
