1 NAME Gaius Julius Plancius Varus Cornutus
2 GIVN Gaius Julius Plancius Varus Cornutus
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gaius Julius Plancius Varus Cornutus was a man of Roman Senatorial rank who lived in the Roman Empire in the 2nd century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornutus was the son and only child of Gaius Julius Cornutus Tertullus and Plancia Magna. His paternal grandparents were the Proconsul and Suffect Consul Gaius Julius Cornutus Tertullus and possibly Tertulla. While his maternal gr
2 CONC andparents were the Roman Senator and Proconsul Marcus Plancius Varus and Herodian Princess Julia. His family were prominent citizens and patrons in Perga.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornutus was of Roman, Jewish, Nabataean, Edomite, Greek, Armenian and Persian ancestry. Through his maternal grandmother, Cornutus’ ancestors were King Archelaus of Cappadocia, King of Judea Herod the Great and his wife Mariamne.
2 CONC  Cornutus along with his mother; maternal uncle Gaius Plancius Varus and his maternal relatives were among the last known descendants of the Herodian Dynasty. He appeared to be an apostate to Judaism. It is unlikely that Cornutus 
2 CONC attempted to exert influence on Judean Politics. He was born and raised in Perga, the capital of the Roman province of Pamphylia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Agora in Perga, the local government in Perga had dedicated and honored Cornutus with an inscription on a statue base. This inscription honors Cornutus and his family. Cornutus and his ancestors are highly praised as the be
2 CONC nefactors of Perga and the inscription states how lawful, considerable and rewarding citizens they were. This inscriptions reveals how prominent he and his family were and shows the respect that the citizens of Perga had for Cornu
2 CONC tus and his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources===
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://www.jstor.org/pss/297430
