2 CONT
2 CONT Shalmaneser IV was king of Assyria (783 - 773 BC). He succeeded his father Adad-nirari III, and was succeeded by his brother Ashur-dan III. Very little information about his reign has survived.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the eponym canon, he led several campaigns against Urartu. His rulership was severely limited by the growing influence of high dignitaries, particularly that of Shamshi-ilu, who was then commander-in-chief of the army
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shalmaneser_IV
