1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Viharamahadevi  (Sinhala:විහාරමහාදේවි) was the mother of King Dutugamunu, Saddhatissa and the Queen consort of King Kavantissa (King of the Ruhuna Sri Lanka). Some scholars suggest that her original name was 'śaver
2 CONC a', which possibly means goddess of the night.
2 CONT
2 CONT Queen Viharamahadevi was the daughter of King Kelanitissa who ruled Kelaniya.[4] The king once punished an innocent monk by boiling him alive in a cauldron of oil. It is said that the gods, angered over this cruel deed, made the o
2 CONC cean rush inland and flood the land. Soothsayers said that if a princess was sacrificed to the sea, the raging waves would stop. The young princess sacrificed herself for the sins of her father and for the safety of her motherland
2 CONC . She was placed inside a beautifully decorated boat which bore the letters Daughter of a King and set adrift on the sea.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is said that as soon as she was sent off, the sea suddenly turned calm again and the water receded. However, the king was very upset, the queen was wailing and the citizens were very angry over the loss of their brave princess.
2 CONC  They all started blaming the king.
2 CONT
2 CONT Meanwhile, the young princess finally reached the shore, at a spot known as Dovera in Kirinda, in the southern part of the country, then known as Rohana (now Ruhuna) which was a quite prosperous area ruled by King Kavantissa. A fi
2 CONC sherman who first spotted the boat is said to have run to the castle, and informed the king about the castaway princess. The Thupavamsa says birds who first spotted the floating boat informed the king.
2 CONT
2 CONT The princess was brought before the king in a procession. The king, on hearing her story, was so impressed that he decided to marry the princess who had been so brave and patriotic to sacrifice her life for her country. As a part 
2 CONC of the legend it's said as she reached the shore at a spot close to the Lanka Vihara, she was named Viharamahadevi. The place where she landed is marked with an inscription laid there by Prince Mahanaga.
2 CONT
2 CONT She bore the king two sons, Dutugemunu and Saddhatissa. The former is one of the greatest heroes of Sri Lanka, while Viharamahadevi herself is recognised as a great heroine of Sri Lanka.
