1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In the Mahabharata epic, Pandu (Sanskrit: पाण्डु Pāṇḍu, lit. yellowish, whitish, pale) was the king of Hastinapur, the son of Ambalika and Vichitravirya. He is popularly known as the father of the Pandavas, who wer
2 CONC e called so after him. Pandu was responsible and a great warrior, who expanded his kingdom during his rule.
2 CONT
