2 CONT SANJAYA WAS LEARNED AND TRUTHFUL. HE TALKED FREELY WITH DHRITARASHTRA AND REPEATED POINTED OUT THAT IT WAS USELESS TO BLAME  FATE WHEN DHIRITARASHTRA HIMSELF WAS RESPONSIBLE FOR HARBOURING GREED  AND FOR NOT KEEPING  DURYYODHANA I
2 CONC N CHECK. ON THE EVE OF THE GREAT MAHABHARATA WAR, HE VISITED THE PANDAVA CAMP AS AN  ENVOY OF KAURAVAS AND UPON HIS RETURN TO HASTINAPURA HE DESCRIBED TO DHRITARASHTRA AND OTHERS, THE STRENGTH  OF THE PANDAVAS AND THEIR DETERMINAT
2 CONC ION TO FIGHT. (5/47-50, 56 57, 68). AFTER THE WAR HE WAS APPOINTED BY YUDHISHTHIRA AS A CHIEF ADMINISTRATOR AND FINANCIAL CONTROLLER OF THE EMPIRE..
