1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gorgo,_Queen_of_Sparta
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gorgo''' (fl. 480 BC) was a Queen of Sparta. She was the daughter and the only known child of Cleomenes I, King of Sparta (r. 520–490 BC) during the 6th and 5th centuries BC. She was the wife of King Leonidas I, Cleomenes' half
2 CONC -brother, who fought and died in the Battle of Thermopylae. Gorgo was also the mother of King Pleistarchus, her only son with co-King Leonidas I. She is also noted as one of the few female historical figures actually named by Hero
2 CONC dotus and was known for her political judgment and wisdom. Her birth date is uncertain, but based on Herodotus' dating, it is most likely to have been between 518 and 508 BC (Histories 5.51).
2 CONT
