1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rusudan,_daughter_of_George_III_of_Georgia
2 CONT
2 CONT Rusudan was the younger daughter of King Giorgi III of Georgia and of his wife, Burdukhan (Gurandukht). Her elder sister was Tamar, who succeeded their father as ruler of Georgia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1158/1160, Rusudan was married, possibly in 1180, to Manuel Komnenos (born 1145), the eldest son of Andronikos I who was to be Byzantine Emperor from 1183 to 1185. Manuel and Rusudan had two sons, Alexios, probably born
2 CONC  in 1182, and David, born around 1184.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Andronikos was deposed and killed, Manuel was blinded, and possibly may have died died from his wounds. It is said that Rusudan fled Constantinople with her sons, taking refuge either in Georgia or in the former Byzantine pro
2 CONC vince of Pontus.
2 CONT
2 CONT While the Fourth Crusade were camped outside Constantinople between 1203 and 1204 (and would later take the city), Tamar sent Georgian troops to help Alexios and David to take control of Pontus in April of 1204. Combined with thei
2 CONC r additional conquests this became the new Empire of Trebizond.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT C. Toumanoff, "On the relationship between the founder of the Empire of Trebizond and the Georgian Queen Thamar" in Speculum vol. 15 (1940) pp. 299–312.
2 CONT
2 CONT Varzos, K. (1984), Ē genealogia tōn Komnēnōn, Thessaloniki, especially vol. 2 p. 515 note 24.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Rusudan, daughter of Giorgi III of Georgia
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Rusudan was the younger daughter of King Giorgi III of Georgia and of his wife, Burdukhan (Gurandukht). Her elder sister was Tamar, who succeeded their father as ruler of Georgia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1158/1160, Rusudan was married, possibly in 1180, to Manuel Komnenos (born 1145), the eldest son of Andronikos I who was to be Byzantine Emperor from 1183 to 1185. Manuel and Rusudan had two sons, Alexios, probably born
2 CONC  in 1182, and David, born around 1184.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Andronikos was deposed and killed Manuel was blinded, and may have died as a result; at any rate he disappears from the historical record. It is said that Rusudan fled Constantinople with her sons, taking refuge either in Geo
2 CONC rgia or in the Pontus.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the Latins seized Constantinople in 1204, Tamar sent Georgian troops to help Alexios and David to take control of the former Byzantine province of Pontus. Combined with their additional conquests this became the new Empire of
2 CONC  Trebizond.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT C. Toumanoff, "On the relationship between the founder of the Empire of Trebizond and the Georgian Queen Thamar" in Speculum vol. 15 (1940) pp. 299-312.
2 CONT
2 CONT Varzos, K. (1984), written at Thessaloniki, Ē genealogia tōn Komnēnōn, especially vol. 2 p. 515 note 24.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Rusudan (Georgian: რუსუდანი; Greek: Ρουσουδάν) was the younger daughter of King George III of Georgia and of his wife, Burdukhan (Gurandukht). Her elder sister was the famous Queen Tamar, who succeeded their father as ruler of Geo
2 CONC rgia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1158/1160, Rusudan was married, possibly in 1180, to Manuel Komnenos (born 1145), the eldest son of Andronikos I, who in turn was to be Byzantine Emperor from 1183 to 1185. Manuel and Rusudan had two sons, Alexios, prob
2 CONC ably born in 1182, and David, born around 1184.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Andronikos was deposed and killed, Manuel was blinded, and possibly may have died from his wounds. It is said that Rusudan fled Constantinople with her sons, taking refuge either in Georgia or in the former Byzantine province
2 CONC  of Pontus.
2 CONT
2 CONT While the Fourth Crusade were camped outside Constantinople between 1203 and 1204 (and would later take the city), Tamar sent Georgian troops to help Alexios and David to take control of Pontus in April 1204. Combined with their a
2 CONC dditional conquests this became the new Empire of Trebizond.
