2 CONT '''Kilij Arslan IV''' (Old Anatolian Turkish: قِلِج اَرسلان, Persian: رکن الدین قلج ارسلان بن کیخسرو‎ Rukn ad-Dīn Qilij Arslān bin Kaykhusraw) was Seljuq Sultan of Rûm after the death of his father Kaykhusraw II in 1246. For part 
2 CONC of his tenure as sultan he ruled with his two brothers Kaykaus II and Kayqubad II. He was executed in 1266 by the Pervane Mu‘in al-Din Suleyman.
