2 CONT 3.         HETHUM (1215-28 Oct 1270, bur Trazarg).  Rüdt-Collenberg cites a colophon of Yovhanes the bishop which names "Beatrice (mother), and Sempad, Hethum, Oshin, Basil, Leo, Vacaghk, Kalamarie, Stephanie and Hripsimeh, virgin
2 CONC  (brothers and sisters), Philipp and Mariam Ibelin (children of Kalamarie)"[981].  The Chronicle attributed to King Hethum II records that "Hetum…son of Kostandin senior paron of the Armenians" succeeded to the Armenian throne in 
2 CONC [24 Jan 1225/23 Jan 1226][982].  His origin, and his marriage, are confirmed by the charter dated 22 Jan 1236 under which "Eython…rex Armenie filius Constantini stirpis regie et Ehelisabeth regina…filia…Leonis regis" granted prope
2 CONC rties to the Teutonic Knights[983].  He succeeded in 1226 on his marriage as HETHUM I King of Armenia.  In 1236 he gave the Teutonic Knights the fief of Haronia, which remained the Order's main territorial grouping outside Palesti
2 CONC ne until well into the 14th century[984].  
2 CONT
