1 CONC .Cunningham and W.W.Tarn claim that the royal profile is that of an older man, and attribute this coinage in Eastern Punjab worshops." (Bopearachchi, "Monnaies Gréco-Bactriennes et Indo-Grecques", p108, translated from the French 
1 CONC original)
