0 @N6000000002188198449@ NOTE Strato I
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Strato I was an Indo-Greek king who ruled between c. 125-110 BCE in Northern India. He was the son of the great king Menander I and his queen Agathokleia, who acted as regent during his early years. The western parts of the Indo-G
1 CONC reek empire, including Paropamisadae and Arachosia, gained independence after the death of Menander I.
1 CONT Contents
1 CONT [hide]
1 CONT
1 CONT     * 1 Territorial losses
1 CONT     * 2 Notes
1 CONT     * 3 See also
1 CONT     * 4 References
1 CONT     * 5 See also
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Territorial losses
1 CONT
1 CONT Strato's territory extended from the mid-Punjab at the Jhelum River in the West to Mathura in the East, retaining the capital of his father in Sagala (modern Sialkot) in the northern Punjab, or possibly to the city of Bucephala (P
1 CONC lutarch, p. 48 n. 5). The area of Gandhara, west of river Jhelum, also belonged to the kingdom but seems to have been lost during the latter part of Strato's reign, perhaps to the Western king Antialcidas. According to archaeologi
1 CONC cal evidence, Strato I was apparently the last Greek king to hold Mathura, which seems to have been lost to Indian kingdoms around 100 BCE.
1 CONT
1 CONT During the life of Strato I, various types of coins were minted, some of them bearing the mention "Dharmika" ("Of the "Dharma") [1].
1 CONT
1 CONT Strato I was also the only Indo-Greek king to appear bearded, probably to indicate that he was no longer an infant.
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Agathokleia Indo-Greek Ruler
1 CONT (Gandhara, Punjab)
1 CONT (125-110 BCE) Succeeded by:
1 CONT Heliokles II
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Notes
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. ?  Legends on the coins of Agathokliea and Strato:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Period 1: Coins where Agathokleia is alone on the obverse, and has a seated Herakles on the reverse:
1 CONT
1 CONT Obverse: Greek BASILISSIS TEOTROPOU AGATOKLEIAS "Queen Agathokleia, Godlike" Reverse: Pali "Maharajasa tratarasa dharmikasa Agathukriae" "Queen Agathokleia, saviour and follower of the dharma"
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Period 2: Coins where only Agathokleia is shown, as regent, with king on the reverse forming the Vitarka Mudra:
1 CONT
1 CONT Obverse: Greek BASILISSIS AGATOKLEIAS ("Queen Agathokleia") Reverse: Pali "Maharajasa tratarasa dharmikasa Stratasa" ("The Great king Strato, saviour and followers of the Dharma")
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Period 3: Coins with Strato as an adolescent, accompanied by Athena peacefully holding Nike
1 CONT
1 CONT Obverse: Greek BASILEOS SOTIROS KAI DIKAIOU STRATONOS "Saviour king Strato, the Just" Reverse: Pali "Maharajasa tratarasa Dhramikasa Stratasa "Great saviour king Strato, follower of the Dharma"
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Period 4: Coins where Strato as an adolescent appears jointly with Agatokleia
1 CONT
1 CONT Obverse: Greek BASILEOS SOTIROS STRATONOS KAI AGATHOKLEIA "Saviour king Strato, and Agathokleia" Reverse: Pali "Maharajasa tratarasa Stratasa/ Agathukriae" "Great saviour king Strato, and Agathokleia"
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Period 5: King Strato alone, with Athena Alkidemos
1 CONT
1 CONT Obverse: Greek BASILEOS SOTIROS STRATONOS "Saviour king Strato" Reverse: Pali "Maharajasa tratarasa Stratasa" "Great saviour king Strato"
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Period 6: King Strato alone, with Athena Alkidemos
1 CONT
1 CONT Obverse: Greek BASILEOS SOTIROS STRATONOS "Saviour king Strato" Reverse: Pali "Maharajasa tratarasa dhramikasa Stratasa" "Great saviour king Strato, follower of the dharma"
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Period 7: King Strato alone, with Athena Alkidemos
1 CONT
1 CONT Obverse: Greek BASILEOS SOTIROS DIKAIOU STRATONOS "Saviour and just king Strato" Reverse: Pali "Maharajasa tratarasa dhramikasa Stratasa" "Great saviour king Strato, follower of the dharma"
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Period 8: King Strato alone, with Athena Alkidemos
1 CONT
1 CONT Obverse: Greek BASILEOS EPIPHANOUS SOTIROS STRATONOS "Saviour and divine king Strato" Reverse: Pali "Maharajasa pracachasa tratarasa Stratasa" "Great saviour king Strato, epiphane"
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] See also
1 CONT
